Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Keep the Qwen referee off the network and out of the run's way

Reason: Two independent faults, one symptom -- a run that dies minutes after
the alignment pass it already paid for, with a traceback that names httpx.

First, `_load_model` hands `from_pretrained` a repository id, and
transformers 5.x resolves the repository's chat-template list over the network
before it consults the cache. The weights are already on disk by then --
`ensure_hf_model` returned cleanly, which is exactly the condition under which
nothing needs fetching. That resolution has an offline fallback and it is not
reached: `list_repo_templates` catches `httpx.NetworkError`, while
`httpx.ConnectTimeout` inherits from `TimeoutException`, its sibling. A
refused connection recovers; a filtered one (`WinError 10060`) raises. Passing
`local_files_only` when the pinned snapshot is vouched for takes the branch
that never asks. Upstream 0.5.0 changed nothing here: the `revision=` pin it
passes has been in place since 0.4.2 and is not what this is about.

Second, `apply_verification` has no containment at either call site: the
referee produces evidence and never decisions, yet any exception out of it
takes the whole pipeline down. Catching under `auto` -- and only under `auto`,
since `on` is a caller asking for the evidence -- removes the blast radius.
The `qwen_verify` key stays unwritten on that path so the later finalization
pass is still willing to try.

The upload connect timeout comes along because it is the same failure mode one
layer up: 45s is spent per resolved address, and
`generativelanguage.googleapis.com` has several, so a filtered host sat silent
for 169 measured seconds before the first retry line -- indistinguishable from
a hang. 15s still clears a working link. Upstream 0.5.0 moved that constant out
of `llm/client.py` into the new `llm/media_upload.py`; the value is unchanged.

Removal: Delete once upstream loads pinned local weights offline (or widens
that fallback to `TimeoutException`) and treats a failed referee pass as
missing evidence rather than a failed run.

